## English summary (for convenience only; the Chinese text governs)

This is a **self-written, permissive open-source license for Layer A** of Fenestra — the kernel, the permission gate / capability arbitration, the plugin runtime, the FEP specification, and the example plugins. It is written to satisfy the substance of the Open Source Definition: free redistribution, source availability, permission to modify, no discrimination against persons, groups, or fields of endeavor (commercial use included), automatic license passage, no product or technology lock-in, and no requirement that combined or derived works be open-sourced. It is **not an OSI-approved license** and must not be called one.

You may use, copy, modify, distribute, sublicense, and commercially exploit Layer A — including inside closed-source products — as long as you keep the copyright and license notice and mark your modifications. You owe no source publication, no contribution back, and no fees.

Two hard commitments bind the copyright holder itself: (1) **any version released under this license can never be re-proprietarized** — its granted rights are permanent and irrevocable, and a later license change never retroactively affects released copies or forks; and (2) **Layer A's API/ABI, the gate itself, and its security invariants (default-deny, least-privilege intersection, sandbox isolation, explicit privacy consent, `Untrusted<T>` outbound revalidation, revertible registration) stay open forever**, and **Layer B commercial plugins may never weaken them, even for paying customers**. Layer B is governed separately by `LICENSE-COMMERCIAL` (Fenestra Source License v1.0). The Chinese text above governs.

